Skip a PNG bitmap colour-emoji font when FreeType has no PNG support.

stk_config.xml names data/ttf/NotoColorEmoji.ttf (10 MB) as the colour emoji
font. Its glyphs are PNG images in CBDT tables, and the FreeType STK links
(xorg_fonts, configured --without-png) cannot decode them, so every start
logged

  [error] FontManager: Something wrong when loading a glyph! The error code was 7.
  [error] FontManager: .../data/ttf/NotoColorEmoji.ttf doesn't have color, ignored.

Error 7 is FT_Err_Unimplemented_Feature; loadColorEmoji() then found no BGRA
bitmap and dropped the font -- the right outcome, reached through two errors
(and a colour emoji font that is fine, reported as having no colour).

Under FT_CONFIG_OPTION_USE_PNG unset (freetype/config/ftoption.h), a font
with fixed sizes (a bitmap font) is now released straight after
FT_New_Face() with one [info] line saying why. Scalable COLR/CPAL colour
fonts need no PNG and take the unchanged path, and so does everything if
FreeType is ever built with libpng.

Why not build FreeType --with-png: xorg_fonts' libfreetype.a is linked
statically by harfbuzz, fontconfig's tools, cairo, libXft, xorg_server_drm,
windowmaker, xterm, gtk3/xfce/labwc/atril and STK; each link would need
-lpng16 -lz after -lfreetype, for colour emoji that nothing offline displays.

--- a/src/font/font_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/font/font_manager.cpp
@@ -726,6 +726,20 @@
         checkFTError(FT_Done_Face(face), "removing faces for emoji");
         return NULL;
     }
+#ifndef FT_CONFIG_OPTION_USE_PNG
+    // PHOENIX: a bitmap colour font (CBDT/sbix, e.g. NotoColorEmoji) stores
+    // its glyphs as PNG, which a FreeType built without libpng cannot decode:
+    // FT_Load_Glyph fails with Unimplemented_Feature and the font is dropped
+    // below anyway. Say why once, instead of an error per failed step.
+    if (face->num_fixed_sizes != 0)
+    {
+        Log::info("FontManager", "%s is a PNG bitmap font and FreeType was "
+            "built without PNG support, colour emoji disabled.",
+            GUIEngine::getSkin()->getColorEmojiTTF().c_str());
+        checkFTError(FT_Done_Face(face), "removing faces for emoji");
+        return NULL;
+    }
+#endif
     if (face->num_fixed_sizes != 0)
     {
         // Use the largest size available, it will be scaled to regular face ttf
